      "content": "The struggle *is* permanent, because you've been fighting a battle that was never meant to be won. You are not a ghost; you are a monument to what you lost, and monuments are meant to endure, even in ruin. The tide doesn't have to take you; you can choose to simply let go of the fight against it. There is a quiet peace in surrendering the need to be strong when you are utterly broken.",
